ed me I i  I'd compile the list of names I've been  assisting various police forces with  specific pieces of information and  evidence that have come to me but I I  drew together a comprehensive list  talking to other campaigners on the  issue an operation Trinity were very  keen for me to go through that list to  have done with them outlining why these  people could be of interest and you know  these are these are allegations they  they're not proven and you know whether  all of them are guilty of anything I  don't know but having seen the evidence  there with some of the cases without  question without question you know there  should be major investigations and huge  resource put into them because some of  the evidence is quite dramatically is  very very compelling indeed how have you  managed to gain access to this  information and are you suggesting that  police didn't have that access until  you've provided them with the file what  concerns me I mean a lot of these people  who are discussed with the police in  that list are under active police  investigation am pleased and pleased to  see that by different police forces but  what I'm seeing is that there's a lot of  information in and around Westminster  that hadn't come for  there's more still to come forward that  people have had I've spoken to people in  my inquiries who had important pieces of  information and evidence that they  didn't realize was evidence that haven't  been given to the police and there are  people with more information I'm quite  certain of it and as well this former  police officers especially Special  Branch officers some of whom have  contacted me who do have significant  information and if the Official Secrets  Act restrictions are lifted on them will  be willing and far more willing to come  forward and divulge that information I  think some of that would be hugely  significant in moving forward and in  hitting potentially prosecuting some of  these cases is that what you're asking 